  "derivation": "P2: w = (500/1000)*24 + (1000/1000)*18 + 10 = 12 + 18 + 10 = 40 kPa; q_net = 200 - 40 = 160 kPa. P1/P3: use service FZ only, ignore the factored row and the moments. F1: max(576,400)/160 = 3.6 m2; 1.8^2 = 3.24 < 3.6 < 4 = 2.0^2, so 2000 mm. F2: 640/160 = 4 = 2.0^2, so 2000 mm exactly. F3: 64/160 = 0.4 m2; 0.6^2 = 0.36 < 0.4 < 0.64 = 0.8^2, but 800 < 900 mm, so round the minimum to 1000 mm. F4: 1600/160 = 10 m2; 3.0^2 = 9 < 10 < 10.24 = 3.2^2; 3200 > 2450 mm, so floor(2450/200)*200 = 12*200 = 2400 mm, LIMIT_REACHED, plan_at_max true. F5 and F7: a service row is zero and negative respectively, hence UPLIFT even with a positive envelope row at F5. F6: only a factored row, hence NO_SERVICE_LOAD. P6: ceil(900/200)*200 = 5*200 = 1000 mm. h = 500 mm and s = 200 mm are the basis values. P5 is the only bound flag set by these cases. Sizes are square, source calc, and successful rows have no reason.",
